  m_Name: KevinPratt
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ResumeData
  applicantName: Dr. Kevin Pratt
  body: '<b>DR. KEVIN PRATT, PhD, MD, ESQ.</b>

    Applying for: Office Manager


    <b>EDUCATION</b>

    {phd}


    <b>EXPERIENCE</b>

    {title}
    - Self-Employed

    {dates}


    <b>CERTIFICATIONS</b>

    {cert}


    <b>REFERENCES</b>

    {ref}'
  claims:
  - id: phd
    text: PhD in Office Management, University of Online (est. last Tuesday)
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 0
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Your university was founded last Tuesday?
      answer: It's a {u_fast} program. I finished my PhD in {u_hours}.
      demeanor: 5
      phrases:
      - id: u_fast
        text: very fast-paced
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Accelerated learning. They mailed the diploma before I applied.
        callOutDemeanor: 5
      - id: u_hours
        text: three hours
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Two hours and fifty minutes, actually. I'm gifted.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: A PhD! Impressive.
      answer: Please, call me Doctor. Or Dr. Kevin. Or simply 'The Doctor'.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: title
    text: Chief Medical Office Manager
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 2
    designerNote: '''Chief'' title with one week of experience breaks rule 5.'
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: '''Chief Medical Office Manager''? Of what office?'
      answer: Of my {k_apartment}. It has an office. And a medicine cabinet.
      demeanor: 4
      phrases:
      - id: k_apartment
        text: apartment
        isContradiction: 1
        callOutResponse: Fine! It's a studio apartment. The 'office' is a chair.
          But I manage that chair VERY well.
        callOutDemeanor: 3
    goodQuestion:
      question: Chief Medical Office Manager sounds important.
      answer: It is. People call me in emergencies. Office emergencies. Like when
        the stapler is empty.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: dates
    text: Last week - Present
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 1
    designerNote: 'Breaks rule 1: needs 2+ years of experience.'
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: You've only had this job since last week?
      answer: '{w_quality} over quantity. It was a very long week.'
      demeanor: 4
      phrases:
      - id: w_quality
        text: Quality
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Quantity is overrated. Ask anyone. Ask me.
        callOutDemeanor: 4
    goodQuestion:
      question: Fresh experience. Exciting.
      answer: Very fresh. It still has that new-job smell.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: cert
    text: Certified Doctor of Paperwork
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 3
    designerNote: No certificate ID breaks rule 4.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Your certification doesn't have an ID number.
      answer: The ID is... {c_id}. Yes. That's it.
      demeanor: 5
      phrases:
      - id: c_id
        text: 1-2-3-4
        isContradiction: 1
        callOutResponse: Okay, I printed it myself. But the printer was very expensive!
          That should count.
        callOutDemeanor: 3
    goodQuestion:
      question: Doctor of Paperwork, nice.
      answer: I've done so much paperwork. Including this certificate. Which I...
        received.
      demeanor: 5
      phrases: []
  - id: ref
    text: Dr. Kevin Pratt
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 5
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: You listed yourself as your own reference.
      answer: Who knows me better? I'd {r_vouch} any day.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: r_vouch
        text: vouch for me
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Call me. I'll pick up. I'll say great things.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: Can your reference speak to your work?
      answer: Absolutely. Here's his number. It's my number. He's very available.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  referenceLetter: 'To whom it may concern,


    I, Dr. Kevin Pratt, {rl_self} confirm
    that Dr. Kevin Pratt is an excellent candidate. He holds {rl_degrees} and is
    very {rl_humble}.


    Yours,

    Dr. Kevin Pratt, PhD, MD, Esq.'
